        "teacherMoves": "Say: \"Take 2 minutes silently to write one thing the histogram taught you and one new question. Then place your note on the DQB.\" WAIT TIME 10-15 seconds before inviting the first learner. Cold-call 3 learners to read a note and say which key inquiry question it connects to. Ask: \"Which question on our board did today's evidence help us answer? Which still needs data?\" Point out that Lesson 7 will draw frequency polygons and compare Thika Road with Mombasa Road. Group similar questions and highlight one that connects to the community presentation in Lesson 8.",
        "sensemakingStrategy": "Driving Question Board as a public record of learning: sorting questions into answered, partly answered and open shows learners how today's evidence moves the class understanding forward and sustains motivation for the next lesson.",
        "formativeAssessment": "Check that notes are specific (for example mention frequency density or the wide class) rather than generic. Count how many learners connect a note to one of the 3 KICD key inquiry questions. Note learners whose questions still reflect the 'mean = safe' idea and plan to address them in Lesson 7 and Lesson 8."
