    "teacherReflection": "After the lesson, reflect: Did learners see the empty 400 to <600 bar and realise that few gaps are near the mean of 400 m? Which groups divided by the class width in metres instead of units of 100 m? Did the wide class genuinely create cognitive conflict, and did frequency density make sense to learners as 'squeezing' a wide class to a fair height? Which learners can read the histogram but cannot yet link it to the pedestrians and the near-miss log? Did the officer remain respected as correct but incomplete? What extra graph paper or pre-labelled axes are needed for Lesson 7?",
