      "skills": "Plotting points on a scale; using midpoints from the grouped table; using a spreadsheet to build a scatter or line chart; comparing graphs. NGSS-aligned practices: Analyzing and Interpreting Data; Using Mathematics and Computational Thinking; Developing and Using Models; Engaging in Argument from Evidence. KICD core competencies: Critical thinking and problem solving (uses frequency polygons to examine data and make conclusions); Digital literacy (uses digital devices to draw frequency polygons); Communication and collaboration.",
      "attitudes": "KICD values: Integrity (plots and records data accurately); Unity (works in groups using collected data to draw frequency polygons). PCIs: Life Skills (Decision Making), as learners make informed decisions from the polygons; Road safety, as learners discuss where pedestrians are at risk. Learners respect Ms Halima Abdi's mean as correct but incomplete.",
