    "overview": "Back at Ruaraka Hills Secondary School on Thika Road, Mwalimu Wanjiru reminds the class that Ms Halima Abdi's mean of 400 m is correct but incomplete, and that Mzee Otieno's log places 9 of 12 near-misses in one stretch. Learners first predict what a line graph of the gap data (20 gaps, Thika Road, classes of width 200 m) will look like and whether two roads with similar means will look similar. They then draw the Thika Road frequency polygon by hand from the midpoints (100, 300, 500, 700, 900, 1100) and frequencies (5, 9, 0, 2, 1, 3), closing it at (-100, 0) and (1300, 0). Groups repeat the process with a spreadsheet and add the Mombasa Road Embakasi data (4, 8, 5, 2, 1, 0; grouped mean 380 m) on the same axes. In the Explain phase they compare hump, tail and spread, and conclude that similar means (440 m and 380 m) hide different shapes: Thika Road has a second small rise at 1000 to <1200 m, while Mombasa Road has no gap of 1000 m or more. The class updates the DQB and the cumulative model.",
